{{also|Marzipan}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|marchpane||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Marzipan}}, from {{der|en|it|marzapane}}, {{der|en|vec|marzapane}}. Believed to be, with influence from {{m|it|pane|t=bread}}, derived from {{der|en|ar|مَرْطَبَان|t=spice box}} which comes from the name of a Burmese port known for its spice exports, {{w|Mottama|Martaban}}, now called in {{cog|my|မုတ္ထမ}}.

