===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Marzipan candy in a store window in Florence.jpg|thumb|fruit-shaped '''marzipan''' at a market in {{l|en|Florence}}, Italy]]
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A [[confection]] made from a [[paste]] of [[almond]]s, [[sugar]] and [[egg white]] as a [[binder]].
# A similar confection made using another [[nut]], such as [[peanut]] or [[hazelnut]].
#* '''2009''', Hamlyn, ''Hamlyn All Colour Cookery: 200 Christmas Recipes: Hamlyn All Colour Cookbook'', Hamlyn ({{ISBN|9780600623014}})
#*: Place the hazelnuts on a baking sheet and grill {{...}} then grind finely {{...}} then add the caster sugar and ground hazelnuts [to egg whites] and mix to a stiff '''marzipan''' paste. Sandwich the pecan nuts together in pairs with a little of the hazelnut '''marzipan'''.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|title=The Oxford Companion to Sugar and Sweets|page=433|publisher=Oxford University Press|isbn=9780199313617
|passage=Hazelnut '''marzipan'''. Hazelnuts are used as an alternative to almonds, ground together in a proportion from 11⁄2 to 2 parts nuts to sugar. Almonds may be mixed in according to taste.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Lagusta Yearwood|title=Sweet + Salty: The Art of Vegan Chocolates, Truffles, Caramels, and More from Lagusta's Luscious|publisher=Da Capo Lifelong Books|isbn=9780738235066
|passage={{...}} cookie mini pack, watermelon Bubble Yum or, my favorite, de la Rosa, a peanut '''marzipan''' round packaged in a cellophane wrapper with a delicate rose printed on it. De la Rosa is a perfect confection. Just crumbly enough, just sweet enough&nbsp;{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Amy C. Evans|author2=Martha Hall Foose|title=A Good Meal Is Hard to Find: Storied Recipes from Deep South|publisher=Chronicle Books|isbn=9781452175935|page=87
|passage=To make the filling: In a food processor, blend the peanut butter, powdered sugar, salt, and cayenne together. {{...}} THE FILLING RECIPE IS ALSO awfully close to that of peanut '''marzipan''', which you can make yourself by adding more powdered sugar to create a sturdier, shape-able “dough,” or just look for the de la Rosa brand at your local Latino grocery.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A piece of such a confection.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Lance Olsen|title=Girl Imagined by Chance|publisher=University of Alabama Press|isbn=9781573661034|page=81
|passage=One afternoon not long afterwards you waited byher bedside as she swam through anesthetic. A box of cherry chocolates and a dozen roses in your lap. Cherry chocolates and chocolate-covered '''marzipans'''. Then you drove her home. Chocolate-covered '''marzipans''' being her favorite.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Rosanna Chiofalo|title=Rosalia's Bittersweet Pastry Shop|publisher=Kensington Books|isbn=9781617739385
|passage=In one hand she held a handkerchief, and in the other she held two cherry-shaped '''marzipans'''. Rosalia smiled when she saw the '''marzipans''' and took them and the handkerchief from Madre Carmela.}}

